## How the chapters relate

Chapters are numbered in the order they were written, which is not the order they
depend on each other. A chapter whose model was copied from an earlier one
declares it in its own `_fork.yml`, and that is what this is drawn from. The
label on each arrow is the axis the fork changed, taken from the two chapters'
`categories:`.

```{python}
#| echo: false
#| output: asis
# GENERATED FROM THE CHAPTERS, never drawn by hand (rule 34 keeps this block).
#
# Reads source, executes none of it: no chapter model is imported or solved, so
# this page stays free to render and has no cross-chapter value dependency.
# `create_chapter` deletes this page's freeze when it scaffolds a chapter,
# because rule 12 cannot -- the root index belongs to no chapter, so nothing
# else would notice a seventh node was missing.
#
# The EDGE LABEL is derived, not written. Every fork in this notebook changes
# exactly one axis of `_categories.yml` -- the file says so itself, "each
# chapter keeps what its parent modelled and adds one thing" -- so the label is
# what the child's categories have that the parent's do not. Deriving it means
# it cannot disagree with the categories, cannot invent a term outside the
# vocabulary rule 36 polices, and is not a third place to keep the same fact.
import pathlib
import re

_TITLE = re.compile(r'^title:\s*"(.+)"\s*$', re.M)
_CATS = re.compile(r"^categories:\s*\[(.+?)\]\s*$", re.M)


def _fork(_d):
    """`_fork.yml`'s parent, or None. Flat by design -- see lint.read_fork."""
    _f = _d / "_fork.yml"
    if not _f.exists():
        return None
    _m = re.search(r"^parent:\s*(.+?)\s*$", _f.read_text(), re.M)
    return _m.group(1).strip() if _m else None


_chapters = sorted(p for p in pathlib.Path("chapters").iterdir() if p.is_dir())
_titles, _cats, _parent = {}, {}, {}
for _c in _chapters:
    _index = _c / "index.qmd"
    _text = _index.read_text() if _index.exists() else ""
    _m = _TITLE.search(_text)
    _titles[_c.name] = _m.group(1) if _m else _c.name
    _m = _CATS.search(_text)
    _cats[_c.name] = ({x.strip().strip('"') for x in _m.group(1).split(",")}
                      if _m else set())
    # Only a parent that still exists: a fork naming a renamed chapter should
    # leave a root node rather than a dangling edge.
    _p = _fork(_c)
    if _p and (pathlib.Path("chapters") / _p).is_dir():
        _parent[_c.name] = _p

_id = lambda s: "c" + re.sub(r"[^0-9A-Za-z]", "", s)
print("```{mermaid}")
print("graph TD")
for _c in _chapters:
    print(f'  {_id(_c.name)}["{_titles[_c.name]}"]')
    print(f"  click {_id(_c.name)} \"chapters/{_c.name}/index.html\"")
for _c in _chapters:
    if _c.name not in _parent:
        continue
    _p = _parent[_c.name]
    _added = sorted(_cats[_c.name] - _cats[_p])
    _edge = f'-->|"{", ".join(_added)}"|' if _added else "-->"
    print(f"  {_id(_p)} {_edge} {_id(_c.name)}")
print("```")
```

